# shakedown-qwen30b — NOT A STUDY MODEL. Do not put it in a results table.
#
# Exists only to shake down the paid path cheaply: weights download onto the persistent
# filesystem, vLLM boot at TP=1, docker grading, teardown, cost ledger. None of that cares
# which weights are loaded, so this uses the smallest checkpoint that still honours the
# study's held constants — in particular MAX_MODEL_LEN=262144, so the run exercises the
# real KV-cache pressure rather than a toy context.
#
# Why the FP8 checkpoint and not the BF16 one, on an 80 GB card:
#
#   BF16   30.5B x 2 bytes            = ~61 GB weights
#          KV @ 262144 tok            = ~24 GiB   (2 x 48 layers x 4 kv-heads x 128 dim x 2B)
#          61 + 24 = 85 GB            > 80 GB     -> vLLM refuses to start
#   FP8    ~31 GB weights + ~24 GiB KV = ~55 GB   -> fits, with headroom for concurrency
#
# So BF16 at the study's context length does not fit one H100 at all. That arithmetic is
# also why the real qwen3-coder-next entry cannot be a 1x H100 model — see its env file.
#
# Verified on HF 2026-09-07: public, apache-2.0, not gated.
HF_REPO="Qwen/Qwen3-Coder-30B-A3B-Instruct-FP8"
HF_REVISION="dcaee4d4dfc5ee71ad501f01f530e5652438fde0"
TP=1
MAX_MODEL_LEN=262144
# vLLM refuses tool_choice:"auto" unless BOTH of these are set, and the harness agent
# loop sends exactly that on every call — so without them no attempt can ever run:
#   HTTP 400: "auto" tool choice requires --enable-auto-tool-choice and
#             --tool-call-parser to be set
# The parser is per-model-family, which is why it lives here rather than in the held
# constants. vLLM 0.28.0 ships one for every model in the study lineup: qwen3_coder,
# kimi_k3, minimax_m3, deepseek_v4, glm47.
EXTRA_ARGS="--enable-auto-tool-choice --tool-call-parser qwen3_coder"
INSTANCE_TYPE="gpu_1x_h100_pcie"
